---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="How this site collects, uses and stores your data: analytics, local storage and service providers.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated: 14 October 2026.</strong></p>
    <p>
      This page explains how the site handles data: analytics, the services
      used to publish the site, and the use of cookies and similar
      browser-storage technologies. In this policy, “cookies” includes local
      storage and other technologies that store information on, or access
      information from, your browser or device.
    </p>

    <h2>Data controller</h2>
    <dl class="privacy-facts surface">
      <div class="privacy-facts__row">
        <dt>Data controller</dt>
        <dd><strong>Niko Karppinen</strong>, site owner (private individual)</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="privacy-facts__row">
        <dt>Contact</dt>
        <dd><span data-contact-email data-user="privacy" data-domain="karppinen.one">privacy [at] karppinen.one</span></dd>
      </div>
      <div class="privacy-facts__row">
        <dt>Right to complain</dt>
        <dd><a href="https://tietosuoja.fi/en">Office of the Data Protection Ombudsman (Finland)</a></dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
      The site's own code does not set traditional HTTP cookies. It uses local
      storage for the functional purposes listed below. No advertising or
      social media cookies are used, and the analytics described below works
      without cookies.
    </p>
    <table>
      <caption>Information stored in your browser's local storage</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Function</th>
          <th scope="col">What is stored</th>
          <th scope="col">Key</th>
          <th scope="col">Stored by and owner</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Theme preference</td>
          <td>Your system, light or dark theme selection.</td>
          <td><code>theme</code></td>
          <td>karppinen.one</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Cookiebot banner styler</td>
          <td>The colours, alignment and other preview settings you choose.</td>
          <td><code>cookiebot-banner-styler</code></td>
          <td>karppinen.one</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>GTM container builder</td>
          <td>Your selected tags, container mode, naming convention and configuration values.</td>
          <td><code>karppinen-gtm-tag-selection-v1</code></td>
          <td>karppinen.one</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Data layer documentation generator</td>
          <td>The contents of your editable document draft.</td>
          <td><code>nk:datalayer-documenter:v1</code></td>
          <td>karppinen.one</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>GA4 annotation tool</td>
          <td>Your chosen language.</td>
          <td><code>ga4-annotation-language</code></td>
          <td>karppinen.one</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Guide checklists</td>
          <td>The items you tick on that guide page.</td>
          <td><code>checklist:</code> + page path</td>
          <td>karppinen.one</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      This information stays in your browser. The site does not upload it to
      a server or share it with third parties. It stays there until you reset
      the relevant tool or clear this site's cookies and stored site data in
      your browser.
    </p>

    <h2>Service providers</h2>
    <p>
      When you open a page, the providers below process technical data such as
      your IP address and your browser's request details so that the page
      loads, stays protected and the statistics work.
    </p>
    <table>
      <caption>Service providers used by the site</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Service</th>
          <th scope="col">Role</th>
          <th scope="col">Data processed</th>
          <th scope="col">Location</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>GitHub Pages (Microsoft)</td>
          <td>Site hosting</td>
          <td>IP address, time of requests, and device and browser details. GitHub is the controller for this processing.</td>
          <td>United States and other GitHub locations</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Cloudflare</td>
          <td>Proxy, DNS and traffic statistics</td>
          <td>IP address and browser request details. Statistics are collected on the server without cookies, and the site owner only sees aggregated figures.</td>
          <td>United States (global network)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Rybbit</td>
          <td>Visitor statistics (see below)</td>
          <td>See the next section</td>
          <td>Germany and Finland (Hetzner)</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      GitHub and Cloudflare are US companies. Transfers rely on the European
      Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses or the EU–US Data Privacy
      Framework. GitHub states that it is certified under the framework. More
      information: <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics (Rybbit)</h2>
    <p>
      The site uses <a href="https://rybbit.com/privacy">Rybbit</a> for
      privacy-focused visitor statistics. Rybbit does not set cookies or store
      anything on your device. Session replay is not used.
    </p>
    <table>
      <caption>Data processed by Rybbit</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Data</th>
          <th scope="col">Stored?</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Pages you view and the referring site</td>
          <td>Yes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Session duration</td>
          <td>Yes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Browser, operating system and screen size</td>
          <td>Yes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Country and region</td>
          <td>Yes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Campaign parameters (UTM)</td>
          <td>Yes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>IP address</td>
          <td>No. It is used only briefly to determine your country and region.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Visitor identifier</td>
          <td>Yes, but it changes daily, so it cannot be used to follow you from one day to the next.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Cookies and local storage</td>
          <td>No</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Session replay</td>
          <td>Not used</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Retention</td>
          <td>5 years, after which the data is deleted automatically</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Your IP address reaches the server as with any website. From the
      statistics I see which content is read and use that to improve the site.
      Traffic passes through Cloudflare's network, so your IP address is also
      briefly visible to Cloudflare. Rybbit processes the data on my behalf under a data
      processing agreement (DPA). More information: <a href="https://rybbit.com/subprocessors">Rybbit's subprocessors</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Fonts, images and other page assets are served from this site's own
      domain. Links to external services
      only take you to those services when you choose to follow them. Their own
      privacy policies then apply.
    </p>

    <h2>Managing stored information</h2>
    <p>
      You can remove locally stored information with a tool's reset function,
      where available, or by clearing the cookies and site data for this domain
      in your browser settings. If you block browser storage, your preferences
      and tool drafts may not be restored on your next visit.
    </p>

    <p>This page will be updated if the site's storage or tracking practices change.</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<script>
  // The address is assembled in the browser so it never sits in the HTML as a ready mailto: link.
  function showContactEmail() {
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-contact-email]").forEach((el) => {
      const address = `${el.dataset.user}@${el.dataset.domain}`;
      const link = document.createElement("a");
      link.href = `mailto:${address}`;
      link.textContent = address;
      el.replaceWith(link);
    });
  }
  document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", showContactEmail);
</script>

<style>
  .privacy-facts {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .privacy-facts__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(8.5rem, 11rem) 1fr;
    gap: 0.25rem 1.5rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.25rem;
  }

  .privacy-facts__row + .privacy-facts__row {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .privacy-facts dt {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
  }

  .privacy-facts dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 36rem) {
    .privacy-facts__row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
